  "grammarExplanation": "Some verbs change their stem vowel when stressed — in every form EXCEPT nosotros and vosotros, which keep the original vowel:\n\n• e → ie: querer (quiero, quieres, quiere… pero queremos, queréis), empezar, entender, preferir\n• o → ue: poder (puedo, puedes, puede… pero podemos, podéis), dormir, volver, contar, encontrar, costar\n• u → ue: jugar (juego, juegas, juega, jugamos, jugáis, juegan) — the only one!\n\nKey patterns:\n• querer + infinitive = to want to do something\n• poder + infinitive = to be able to / can do something\n• quedar = to meet up\n• café solo = black coffee",
  "vocabulary": {
    "quedar": {
      "mnemonic": "Stay put and we'll meet there.",
      "explanation": "To meet up / arrange to meet (very common in Spain)."
    },
    "conducir": {
      "mnemonic": "Conduct your car.",
      "explanation": "To drive (Peninsular Spanish; not 'manejar')."
    },
    "llover": {
      "mnemonic": "Llover = water pouring over.",
      "explanation": "To rain."
    },
    "andaluz": {
      "mnemonic": "Andalusia's accent.",
      "explanation": "Andalusian — the accent of southern Spain."
    },
    "aparcamiento": {
      "mnemonic": "Appar-CAr-miento: where cars park.",
      "explanation": "Parking / car park (Peninsular Spanish)."
    },
    "pádel": {
      "mnemonic": "Tennis's Spanish obsession.",
      "explanation": "Padel, the racket sport Spain is mad about."
    },
    "moda": {
      "mnemonic": "In fashion = en moda.",
      "explanation": "Fashion. Estar de moda = to be trendy."
    }
  },
